# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build-context filter for deploy/backend.Dockerfile
#
# BuildKit looks for "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" next to the Dockerfile and
# prefers it over the context-root .dockerignore. That is why this file lives in
# deploy/ and is named after the Dockerfile it belongs to.
# Requires BuildKit (default for `docker compose` v2+ / `docker buildx build`).
#
# Rule: ignore everything, then re-add only what the backend build needs.
# deploy/backend-entrypoint.sh is re-added because the runtime stage COPYs it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*

!backend/
!deploy/backend-entrypoint.sh

# ---- never ship build output or local state into the context ---------------
# Gradle (the wrapper JAR itself must stay — do NOT ignore backend/gradle/)
backend/**/build/
backend/**/.gradle/
backend/**/out/
# Maven (kept in case the backend ever switches wrappers)
backend/**/target/
# JVM crash dumps / profiler output
backend/**/hs_err_pid*.log
backend/**/*.hprof
# local-only Spring config — production config comes from environment variables
backend/**/application-local.*
backend/**/*.db
backend/**/*.db-shm
backend/**/*.db-wal

# ---- secrets / env ---------------------------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.jks
**/*.key

# ---- vcs / editor / os -----------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.iml
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
